---
import ReferenceLayout from '../../components/ReferenceLayout.astro';

const contents = [
  { href: '#legal-1', label: '1. Status and scope' },
  { href: '#legal-2', label: '2. Privacy information' },
  { href: '#legal-2-1', label: '2.1 Local project data' },
  { href: '#legal-2-2', label: '2.2 Build authorization' },
  { href: '#legal-2-3', label: '2.3 Network activity' },
  { href: '#legal-2-4', label: '2.4 Third parties' },
  { href: '#legal-2-5', label: '2.5 Support information' },
  { href: '#legal-2-6', label: '2.6 Retention and deletion' },
  { href: '#legal-2-7', label: '2.7 Website storage' },
  { href: '#legal-2-8', label: '2.8 Future services' },
  { href: '#legal-3', label: '3. Projects and use' },
  { href: '#legal-4', label: '4. Planned pricing' },
  { href: '#legal-5', label: '5. Availability' },
  { href: '#legal-6', label: '6. Third-party software' },
  { href: '#legal-7', label: '7. Information still required' },
];
---

<ReferenceLayout
  pageTitle="Draft legal terms | cppMax"
  metaDescription="Numbered draft beta terms and privacy information for cppMax and this website."
  heading="Draft legal terms."
  introduction="Numbered beta terms and privacy details for reference. These are not final App Store terms."
  contents={contents}
>
  <p class="temporary-note">Draft updated August 31, 2026. Several legally required details are not available yet and are listed in section 7.</p>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-1">
    <details open>
      <summary><span>1</span><h2>Status and scope</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-1-1"><h3><span>1.1</span> Current beta</h3><p>cppMax is pre-release software provided for testing. A beta feature may change, stop working, or be removed before public release.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-1-2"><h3><span>1.2</span> Website</h3><p>This website describes the current beta and planned v1 product. Planned capabilities, prices, and terms are not a purchase offer.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-1-3"><h3><span>1.3</span> Backups</h3><p>Keep a separate backup of important projects. Do not treat the beta as the only copy of critical work.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-2">
    <details open>
      <summary><span>2</span><h2>Privacy information</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-1"><h3><span>2.1</span> Local project data</h3><p>The editor reads and writes project files on the user's device. LLVM, Clang, and LLD process source files locally. The normal edit, compile, and run loop does not require source code, project files, or compiled executables to be sent to a cppMax compiler server.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-2"><h3><span>2.2</span> Build authorization data</h3><p>cppMax uses an executable's SHA-256 hash to identify an exact build for authorization. The current beta provides interpreter access without payment. The final policy has not yet specified whether authorization records are stored only on the device or also by a service, nor has it specified their retention period.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-3"><h3><span>2.3</span> Network activity</h3><p>Core editing and compilation can work offline. A connection may be used for a user-requested Git clone, pull, or push; opening a support channel or public issue tracker; obtaining app or beta updates; and future advertising, envToken, subscription, or payment functions.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-4"><h3><span>2.4</span> Third-party services</h3><p>A Git host receives repository requests when the user connects to that host. An email provider processes messages sent to cppMax contact addresses. Future TestFlight, App Store, advertising, and payment providers may process information under their own terms and privacy policies. Final providers have not all been selected or disclosed.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-5"><h3><span>2.5</span> Support information</h3><p>A user chooses the information included in an email or in-app feedback report. Reports should exclude source code, credentials, private file paths, signing data, and personal information unless the information is needed to investigate the reported issue. Support messages may be sent to support@cppmax.com, manual app reports to feedback@cppmax.com, and other messages to contact@cppmax.com.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-6"><h3><span>2.6</span> Retention and deletion</h3><p>Local project files remain under the user's control and can be removed through the device's file controls or app interface where available. Retention and deletion rules for future server-side authorization, advertising, subscription, payment, or support records have not yet been defined.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-7"><h3><span>2.7</span> Website storage and analytics</h3><p>The website source currently contains no account form, advertising integration, or client-side analytics integration. Hosting infrastructure may produce technical request logs. The hosting provider, log fields, and retention period have not yet been identified in this draft.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-2-8"><h3><span>2.8</span> Planned post-beta services</h3><p>Planned v1 options include optional advertising used to obtain envTokens, a monthly subscription, and prepaid interpreter access. These services are not part of the current beta. Their final data categories, providers, legal bases, retention periods, and user controls must be added before launch.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-3">
    <details>
      <summary><span>3</span><h2>Projects and acceptable use</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-3-1"><h3><span>3.1</span> Project ownership</h3><p>Users keep ownership of code and files they create or import. Users are responsible for having permission to use third-party code, libraries, and repositories.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-3-2"><h3><span>3.2</span> Prohibited use</h3><p>Do not use cppMax or related services to violate applicable law, access systems without permission, distribute malware, or infringe another person's rights.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-4">
    <details>
      <summary><span>4</span><h2>Planned pricing</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-4-1"><h3><span>4.1</span> Beta price</h3><p>The current beta is free.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-4-2"><h3><span>4.2</span> Post-beta model</h3><p>The current plan uses one envToken for standard interpreter entry and two for future graphical programs. An unchanged authorized build may run repeatedly. The editor and compiler are planned to remain free of advertising.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-4-3"><h3><span>4.3</span> Price estimates</h3><p>The likely monthly subscription price is €3.99. The prepaid price is not yet known. All prices, token costs, advertising availability, and prepaid terms may change before release.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-5">
    <details>
      <summary><span>5</span><h2>Availability and beta risk</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-5-1"><h3><span>5.1</span> No uptime promise</h3><p>Beta access and uptime are not guaranteed. Features and supported operations may change during testing.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-5-2"><h3><span>5.2</span> Critical use</h3><p>Do not rely on the beta as the only tool or copy for critical work, and do not use it in a safety-critical system.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-6">
    <details>
      <summary><span>6</span><h2>Third-party software</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-6-1"><h3><span>6.1</span> Open-source tools</h3><p>cppMax includes open-source development tools, including LLVM, Clang, and LLD. Their licenses continue to apply.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-subsection" id="legal-6-2"><h3><span>6.2</span> Connected services</h3><p>Third-party services connected by the user remain subject to their own terms and policies.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="legal-7">
    <details open>
      <summary><span>7</span><h2>Information still required</h2><b aria-hidden="true">+</b></summary>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>Before public release, the final terms and privacy policy must add the operator's legal identity and address, a contact method, governing law, applicable consumer terms, warranty and liability language, termination rules, App Store provisions, processing purposes and legal bases, user rights, the applicable supervisory authority, complete provider and international-transfer disclosures, and record-retention periods.</p>
        <p>The current contact status is listed on the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</ReferenceLayout>

<script>
  const openLinkedSection = () => {
    if (!window.location.hash) return;
    const target = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(window.location.hash);
    target?.closest('details')?.setAttribute('open', '');
  };

  openLinkedSection();
  window.addEventListener('hashchange', openLinkedSection);
</script>

<style>
  :global(.reference-content .legal-block) { padding: 0 !important; scroll-margin-top: 112px; }
  :global(.legal-block details) { border: 0; }
  :global(.legal-block summary) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 42px 1fr 30px; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 34px 0; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; }
  :global(.legal-block summary::-webkit-details-marker) { display: none; }
  :global(.legal-block summary > span) { color: #78b8ff; font: 700 .76rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  :global(.legal-block summary h2) { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 3rem); }
  :global(.legal-block summary b) { color: #78b8ff; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 400; transition: transform 150ms ease; }
  :global(.legal-block details[open] summary b) { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  :global(.legal-body) { padding: 0 0 52px 54px; }
  :global(.legal-subsection) { scroll-margin-top: 112px; padding: 25px 0; border-top: 1px solid #454649; }
  :global(.legal-subsection h3) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 52px 1fr; margin: 0 0 15px; font-size: 1.18rem; }
  :global(.legal-subsection h3 span) { color: #78b8ff; font: 700 .72rem/1.7 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  :global(.reference-content a) { color: #78b8ff; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { :global(.legal-body) { padding-left: 0; } }
</style>
